    {
      "heading": "The volume rule",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Volume equals area of the cross-section times height.",
          "write": "V = A × h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Height is the distance between the two ends.",
          "write": "h = distance between ends"
        },
        {
          "say": "If the prism lies on its side, that height is its length.",
          "write": "lying down: h = length"
        },
        {
          "say": "For a rectangular prism, A is l times w. So V is l w h.",
          "write": "V = l × w × h",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Rectangular prism",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 110,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 140,
                "fill": "blue",
                "change": "highlight",
                "label": "A = l × w"
              },
              {
                "kind": "polygon",
                "points": [
                  [
                    80,
                    110
                  ],
                  [
                    150,
                    50
                  ],
                  [
                    350,
                    50
                  ],
                  [
                    280,
                    110
                  ]
                ],
                "fill": "teal"
              },
              {
                "kind": "polygon",
                "points": [
                  [
                    280,
                    110
                  ],
                  [
                    350,
                    50
                  ],
                  [
                    350,
                    190
                  ],
                  [
                    280,
                    250
                  ]
                ],
                "fill": "teal"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 180,
                "y": 280,
                "text": "l",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "w",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 185,
                "text": "h",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Triangular prism",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Triangle end with base 6 and height 4. The prism is 10 long.",
          "write": "b = 6, h = 4, length 10",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/volume-of-prisms-and-cylinders-ex1.svg",
          "alt": "Triangular prism with base 6 cm, height 4 cm and length 10 cm"
        },
        {
          "say": "Area first. Half times 6 times 4 is 12 square centimetres.",
          "write": "A = ½ × 6 × 4 = 12 cm²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Times by the length. 12 times 10 is 120.",
          "write": "V = 12 × 10 = 120 cm³"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check. The box around it is 240. The prism is half of that.",
          "write": "6 × 4 × 10 = 240, half ✓",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Triangle is half the rectangle",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 120,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 320,
                "h": 180,
                "fill": "white",
                "color": "grey"
              },
              {
                "kind": "polygon",
                "points": [
                  [
                    120,
                    240
                  ],
                  [
                    440,
                    240
                  ],
                  [
                    120,
                    60
                  ]
                ],
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 280,
                "text": "prism = half the box",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Cylinders",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A cylinder has two identical circle ends.",
          "write": "cylinder",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/volume-of-prisms-and-cylinders-cylinder.svg",
          "alt": "Cylinder with radius r and height h"
        },
        {
          "say": "The cross-section is a circle, with area pi r squared.",
          "write": "A = πr²"
        },
        {
          "say": "So volume is pi r squared h.",
          "write": "V = πr²h"
        },
        {
          "say": "Radius 3, height 10. Pi times 9 times 10 is 90 pi.",
          "write": "V = 90π",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/volume-of-prisms-and-cylinders-ex2.svg",
          "alt": "Cylinder radius 3 cm height 10 cm"
        },
        {
          "say": "Use the pi button. That's about 282.7 cubic centimetres.",
          "write": "≈ 282.7 cm³"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Units and capacity",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "One cubic centimetre is one millilitre.",
          "write": "1 cm³ = 1 mL"
        },
        {
          "say": "1000 cubic centimetres make a litre. A cubic metre holds 1000 litres.",
          "write": "1000 cm³ = 1 L, 1 m³ = 1000 L",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 270,
            "alt": "Volume and capacity units",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 120,
                "h": 120,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "1 cm³"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 100,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "= 1 mL",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 220,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 150,
                "h": 150,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "1000 cm³"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 295,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "= 1 L",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "teal"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 130,
                "h": 170,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "1 m³"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 485,
                "y": 240,
                "text": "= 1000 L",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "orange",
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "A tank has diameter 1.2 metres. Halve it. Radius is 0.6.",
          "write": "r = 1.2 ÷ 2 = 0.6 m"
        },
        {
          "say": "Pi times 0.36 times 1.5 is about 1.6965 cubic metres.",
          "write": "V ≈ 1.6965 m³"
        },
        {
          "say": "Times 1000. About 1696 litres.",
          "write": "≈ 1696 L"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Use the area of the cross-section, not a side length.",
          "write": "find A first"
        },
        {
          "say": "The cross-section is the face that stays the same all through.",
          "write": "the same all the way"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't use the diameter. Halve it first.",
          "write": "✗ d   ✓ r = d ÷ 2",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "Use the radius, not the diameter",
            "items": [
